; Stage 1 of doc/rfc/draft-ndn-maru-typed-tree-matching-00.md: what we're building, how each piece relates to
; the others, and what would show it works.
;
; A Check is something the system can be asked.  Its answers are worlds of the plan's chain, in notes/plan/tree-matching.answers:
; `make check` records each case it ran there, and notes/plan/record what observe.l asks (measures, grammars, laws), each
; answer an Evidence value naming the code it ran against.  A check's state reads its latest answer and its last good
; one, both kept by `observed`.  An answer counts only for the code it ran against: plan-world.l makes `Now`, this tree, so
; a capability is proven only if its checks hold now.  Plans never run a check: rules read what's recorded.

start-world plan.
load "notes/plan/probes.l".

; what a check can answer: a law's verdict says more than yes or no
set Evidence = untested | passed(tree) | failed(tree)
  | tested(tree, trials) | proved(tree, cases) | refuted(tree, counterexample) | starved(tree, met, drawn)
  | vacuous(tree) | inconclusive(tree, input).
group Good passed tested proved.

group Check Case Measure Grammar Law.
create Case evidence last-good.                                 ; a case in check/check.l
create Measure evidence last-good command cadence.              ; a program; its exit status is the answer
create Grammar evidence last-good file class rule host inherits samples.  ; compiled live, reading its own language
create Law evidence last-good file support.                     ; one law, by name, of a law file

qualify Case observe is it case-passes.
qualify Measure observe is it command-succeeds.
qualify Grammar observe is it compiles-and-reads.
qualify Law observe is it law-verdict.

; which checks a plain `record` asks; `record full` asks them all
qualify Check routine if 1 = 1.
qualify Measure routine if its cadence = "routine".

; first, because what a whole run shows counts for the cases below, and they then needn't run again
make Measure WholeSuite untested untested "nice make check" "full".
make Measure Erosion untested untested "./eval notes/plan/erosion-hotspots.l" "full".

make Case tree_selectors untested untested.
make Case tree_source untested untested.
make Case tree_lists untested untested.
make Case tree_args untested untested.
make Case tree_args_unread untested untested.
make Case tree_text_refuses untested untested.
make Case tree_interleave untested untested.
make Case tree_apply untested untested.
make Case tree_memo untested untested.
make Case tree_foreign untested untested.
make Case tree_literals untested untested.
make Case tree_parse_complete untested untested.
make Case tree_calc untested untested.

make Measure TextMatchingSpeed untested untested "notes/plan/speed" "routine".

make Grammar CExpressions untested untested "cexpr.g" "<cexpr>" "expression" "" [ ] [ "notes/plan/samples/cexpr.txt" ].
make Grammar JohnPrograms untested untested "john.g" "<john>" "program" "john.l" [ CExpressions ]
  [ "check/john/hanoi2.john", "check/john/x86-allocator.john", "check/john/airline.john" ].
make Grammar LawFiles untested untested "law.g" "<law>" "program" "law-compile.l" [ CExpressions ] [ "check/laws/cexpr.law" ].
make Grammar IrlPrograms untested untested "irl.g" "<irl>" "program" "compile-irl.l" [ CExpressions ] [ "test.irl", "dimacs.irl" ].
make Grammar Arm64Table untested untested "arm64.g" "<arm64spec>" "file" "" [ ] [ "arm64.spec" ].
make Grammar X86Table untested untested "x86.g" "<x86spec>" "file" "" [ ] [ "x86.spec" ].
make Grammar OsDefinitions untested untested "osdefs.g" "<osdefs>" "file" "compile-osdefs.l" [ ] [ "system.osdefs" ].
make Grammar TpegItself untested untested "tpeg.g" "<tpeg>" "parser_spec" "" [ ] [ "cexpr.g", "john.g" ].

make Law conditional_right untested untested "check/laws/cexpr.law" "".
make Law minus_left untested untested "check/laws/cexpr.law" "".
make Law comment_blank untested untested "check/laws/cexpr.law" "".

; an answer says which code gave it, and it's only good for that code
create Code tree.
action Check observed Answer consequence its evidence = Answer and its last-good = Answer if Answer is Good.
; a check's state is what the world holds (doc/rfc/draft-ndn-maru-john-development-00.md): its latest answer, and the
; last good one, which observed keeps, so nothing is worked out again from the answers before
qualify Check holds if its evidence is Good and its evidence tree = Now tree.
qualify Check failing if not its evidence is Good and not its evidence is untested and its evidence tree = Now tree.
qualify Check regressed if it failing = yes and its last-good is Good.
qualify Check stale if not its evidence is untested and not its evidence tree = Now tree.
qualify Check untested if its evidence is untested.

; ---- what we're building
create Capability what where shown-by builds-on planned.

make Capability InputSelectors "a grammar reads its input only through in-head, in-tail and the other input selectors"
  "input.l" [ tree_selectors ] [ ] no.
make Capability AnySource "a grammar can match any source, each stream cell holding its head, lazy tail and memos"
  "source-parser.l" [ tree_source ] [ InputSelectors ] no.
make Capability ListPatterns "a rule can descend into a list and match inside it, as OMeta's form: does"
  "compile-tpeg.l, tpeg.g" [ tree_lists ] [ AnySource ] no.
make Capability ArgsOnInput "a rule's arguments are cells prepended to the stream on a source; on text they stay method arguments"
  "compile-tpeg.l" [ tree_args, tree_args_unread, tree_text_refuses ] [ ListPatterns ] no.
make Capability LiveGrammars "grammars compile in process, so code and grammar blocks can interleave on one input, and every grammar in the tree still compiles live and reads its language"
  "tpeg-repl.l, compile-tpeg.l" [ tree_interleave, conditional_right, minus_left, comment_blank, CExpressions, JohnPrograms, LawFiles, IrlPrograms, Arm64Table, X86Table, OsDefinitions, TpegItself ] [ AnySource ] no.
make Capability ApplyAndSuper "a rule named at run time can be applied, and an override can call its parent's rule"
  "compile-tpeg.l" [ tree_apply ] [ ArgsOnInput, LiveGrammars ] no.
make Capability MemosOnStream "the memo table lives on the stream, so a rule's answer is shared by whoever reads that cell"
  "source-parser.l" [ tree_memo ] [ ListPatterns ] no.
make Capability ForeignRules "a grammar can call another grammar's rule on the same input, with fresh memos, through a proxy cell"
  "source-parser.l, compile-tpeg.l" [ tree_foreign ] [ MemosOnStream ] no.
make Capability OneMatcherForAll "literals in a rule match what the source holds, and a file's grammar must parse completely"
  "compile-tpeg.l, tpeg.g" [ tree_literals, tree_parse_complete ] [ AnySource ] no.
make Capability EndToEnd "a calculator written as a grammar over trees runs with memos and arguments together"
  "check/tpeg-calc.l" [ tree_calc ] [ MemosOnStream, ArgsOnInput ] no.
make Capability TextStaysFast "text matching pays nothing for all this: within 15% of main's"
  "text-parser.l" [ TextMatchingSpeed ] [ AnySource ] no.
make Capability NothingElseBroke "every other check in the repository still passes"
  "the whole tree" [ WholeSuite ] [ EndToEnd, ForeignRules ] no.

; ---- how the pieces relate
; nothing shown is nothing proven
qualify Capability proven if its shown-by size > 0 and for every its shown-by do each holds = yes.
qualify Capability done if it proven = yes or it planned = yes.
qualify Capability ready if for every its builds-on do each done = yes.
qualify Capability regressing if for some its shown-by do each regressed = yes.
qualify Capability failing if for some its shown-by do (each failing = yes and each regressed = no).
qualify Capability aging if for some its shown-by do each stale = yes.
qualify Capability untried if for some its shown-by do each untested = yes.
rel-qualify Capability:A depends-on Capability:B if B in A builds-on.
rel-qualify Check:C supports Capability:K if C in K shown-by.

; ---- what the history says, for reading, never for planning
qualify Check observed-within: N if
  for some time A after (time - N) up to time do (at time A it did observed).

; ---- the goal
create Team.
make Team T.
action Team build Capability consequence Capability planned = yes.
create Hotspot callable file line cc mass tree planned.	; a callable over CC 10 (erosion-run.l --hotspots), for this code
qualify Hotspot current if its tree = Now tree.
action Team simplify Hotspot consequence Hotspot planned = yes.
rule Team simplify is Hotspot current = yes.
rule Team simplify is Hotspot planned = no.
rule Team build is Capability done = no.
rule Team build is Capability ready = yes.
goal Team deliver try for every all Capability do each done = yes.
; what the next step is worth: a regression first, then a failure, then answers about older code, then what's untried,
; and less erosion: each hotspot left costs its mass
heuristic Team deliver 10000 maximize (select all Capability by which planned = yes and which regressing = yes) size.
heuristic Team deliver 1000 maximize (select all Capability by which planned = yes and which failing = yes) size.
heuristic Team deliver 100 maximize (select all Capability by which planned = yes and which aging = yes) size.
heuristic Team deliver 10 maximize (select all Capability by which planned = yes and which untried = yes) size.
heuristic Team deliver 1 minimize total (select all Hotspot by which planned = no and which current = yes) by which mass.
; every capability, in some order that respects builds-on: no choice to search among
goal-strategy Team deliver sat.
